<title>USA: US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 58 in March.</title>
<headline>US Home Builders-Market Index rose to 58 in March.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Home Builders said on Monday its Housing Market Index rose four points to 58 in March from 54 in February.</p>
<p>Builders' ratings of single-family home sales jumped six points, to 61 in March.</p>
<p>A Housing Market Index over 50 generally means positive responses from builders exceeded negative responses. The February index is based on the ratings of 380 respondents.</p>
<p>Traffic of prospective buyers advanced to 49 in March from 46 in February, while the component index for single-family sales in the next six months slipped one point to 67.  </p>
